I know. You see me side-eyeing my book. I was like, what's my book called again? Jared's book follows the aftermath of the disaster at the Kingston coal plant. And in doing so, his book reveals an even larger, ongoing American tragedy. How the TVA started out as a mission-driven public institution, but ended up acting like a private for-profit company. And what that shift can tell us about the consequences of privatization. The story of TVA really begins in many respects

