one of which was to establish a power company, the Tennessee Valley Authority. In 1933, we started. Down on the Tennessee River, when Congress created the Tennessee Valley Authority, an authority commissioned to develop navigation, flood control, agriculture, and industry in the valley. It was, for almost a quarter century, the single most ambitious public work project in the world. Its mission was to lift the rural South out of poverty by making electricity more accessible to all. TVA had three basic goals.

