and brutalist concrete buildings. Shortly after the TVA Act of 1933 is passed, TVA rushes to start building hydroelectric dams throughout the Tennessee Valley. And the first one that they complete themselves from start to finish is Norris Dam outside of Knoxville. First came the dams. Up on the clench at the head of the river. We built Norristown a great barrier to hold water in flood time

