but it's kind of a godsend for them. What they didn't know was that this job came at a huge cost to their health. And turns out these workers had asked for respirators and dust masks throughout the cleanup, and in most cases were not given them. And so they had inhaled this coal ash sludge, and coal ash contains arsenic and radium and mercury,

